  "slug": "noise-quantum-01a5",
  "summary": "New work targets the classical stack of fault-tolerant machines: microsecond GPU decoding, loss-aware decoders, verified compilers, speculation and trapped-ion QEC simulation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is classical software and control that must keep pace with, or resource-optimize, fault-tolerant quantum computation. On decoding, a GPU decoder for bivariate bicycle codes sustains one syndrome round per microsecond under circuit-level noise, and a loss-aware CNN decoder with a fast sampler reduces logical error rates for qubit loss in surface and high-rate qLDPC codes. On compilation, QBlue is extended to block-encoding algorithms with machine-checked verification, and LLM-driven search cuts the expected Toffoli count for RSA-2048 factoring by up to 78.6%. Froq adds safe speculative execution on live quantum states through recovery contracts, while THeatA models transport and heating in QCCD trapped-ion QEC. Hardware-aware and verifiable design is the common emphasis.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
